ts\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s139\",\"d1\",3868,4267,\"Non-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nHome\\nResearch & Innovation\\nGrants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s140\",\"d1\",4267,4644,\"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nHow to apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s141\",\"d1\",4644,5043,\"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s142\",\"d1\",5043,5404,\"Both PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s143\",\"d1\",5404,5672,\"Note: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s144\",\"d1\",5672,5924,\"Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s145\",\"d1\",5924,6311,\"Extending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. ​You can see a full list of these countries on our page about extending the reach of EHA Grants.\\nIf you have questions about your eligibility, you can contact us at [email protected] before submitting an application.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s146\",\"d1\",6311,6631,\"What an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant covers\\nTo reflect the collaborative spirit of the grant, the budget must be divided 50:50 between the two PIs. If this is not the case, a justification must be provided. In any case, no more than 70% of the total grant should be allocated to one PI.\\nYou can use your grant for:\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s147\",\"d1\",6631,6988,\"Personnel costs, including the applicant or the costs of hiring other research staff to work directly on the project\\nLab consumables\\nSmall equipment\\nMiscellaneous expenses, such as publication of your project’s results\\nYou must use some of your grant to pay for:\\nAttendance at the EHA Congress whilst your project is active (maximum €2,000 per PI per year)\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s148\",\"d1\",6988,7367,\"A final audit of your project’s financial costs (maximum €2,000 per PI)\\nYou cannot use your grant to cover:\\nOverhead costs\\nExcessive travel costs\\nCosts that are covered by another fund, even if new funding is acquired during the project, that make all or part of the grant redundant\\nIf you acquire additional funding, you must email us about this within 30 days of its awarding. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s149\",\"d1\",7367,7759,\"You must also tell us how you’ll use the grants together.\\nApply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant Review and Selection Process\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nHow to apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s150\",\"d1\",7759,8140,\"EHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nJoin EHA\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\n60-day trial\\nGet involved\\nCareer development\\nScientific meetings\\nAbout us\\nMission and vision\\nJobs\\nSponsor EHA\\nContact us\\nFollow us\\nPrivacy statement\\nTerms and conditions\\nSubscribe\\nCopyright © 2026\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s151\",\"d1\",8140,8228,\"EHA Mentorship Program\\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\\nApply by October 29\\nApply today\",\"document\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"SUPPLY project involving EHA\",\"time_scope\":\"project duration\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"web-eaa3dae72365a723851945ca\",\"time_metadata\":{}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"]}"
