ing opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nMenu\\nClose\\nConnect & Network\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2027 registration\\nEHA2027 program\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s158\",\"d1\",2310,2710,\"EHA2027 abstract submission\\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\\nEHA2027 sustainability\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress platform\\nEHA2026 sustainability\\nCongress archive\\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\\nEHA2026 gallery\\nEHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\\nEHA2025 gallery\\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\\nEHA2024 report\\nEHA2024 gallery\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s159\",\"d1\",2710,3076,\"EHA2023 report\\nEHA2023 gallery\\nScientific meetings\\nMembership\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\nTrial membership\\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\\nEmeritus membership\\nJoint EHA and national society membership\\nUsing MyEHA\\nClinical practice\\nOur guidelines initiative\\nGuidelines by areas of disease\\nEHA Guidelines app\\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webinar Series\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s160\",\"d1\",3076,3457,\"Bedside Hematology – Rapid Reference\\nEducation & Training\\nEHA Campus\\nLearning paths\\nEuropean Hematology Curriculum\\nEntrustable Professional Activities\\nLighting the Flame Program\\nTests and tools\\nEHA Diagnosis\\nEHA Exam\\nProgress Test\\nMentoring and career development\\nCareer comparison tool\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nMaster Class\\nResearch training programs\\nEHA-EMBO Lab Leadership Course\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s161\",\"d1\",3457,3846,\"Research & Innovation\\nHemaSphere\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\\nSWG Grants\\nHow to apply to join an SWG\\nWebinars and online groups\\nSWG Preceptorship Program\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s162\",\"d1\",3846,4244,\"Scope of our grants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nHome\\nResearch & Innovation\\nGrants\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n4 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s163\",\"d1\",4244,4567,\"How to apply for an EHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nPlease be advised that the call for applications for the 2027 cycle will not open this year. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s164\",\"d1\",4567,4955,\"If you would like to be notified when the next application cycle opens, please join our mailing list by contacting us at [email protected].\\nEHA Innovation Grants encourage and support the:\\nCreation of consortia\\nGeneration of preliminary data that can then be used to apply for larger funding opportunities\\nThe grants:\\nSupport high-quality clinical or translational research in hematology\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s165\",\"d1\",4955,5338,\"Last for a period of two years\\nCan provide a total award of up to €300,000 for the whole consortium\\nEligibility\\nEvery principal investigator (PI) must be an EHA member.\\nAll PIs must be conducting high-quality clinical or translational research. Basic and/or translational researchers can also be included, but the general focus of the project must remain clinical and translational.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s166\",\"d1\",5338,5585,\"All PIs must be independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents in Europe.\\nEach consortium must include at least three PIs operating in at least three different countries in Europe.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s167\",\"d1\",5585,5898,\"At least one of the PIs must operate in of the following countries: Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Estonia, Georgia, Hungary, Kosovo, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Serbia, Slovak Republic, Slovenia, Türkiye, Ukraine.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s168\",\"d1\",5898,6153,\"At least one of the PIs must be a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research.\\nThe outcomes of your project must serve as the basis for applying to larger research projects (e.g. HORIZON EUROPE, EIC ACCELERATOR). \",\"document\",[]],[\"s169\",\"d1\",6153,6405,\"For this reason, you must indicate in your research proposal what funding opportunity you’ll target using the data from your grant-supported project.\\nYou must state a connection to one or more EHA Specialized Working Groups (SWGs) in your application. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s170\",\"d1\",6405,6773,\"For example, as part of your application, you might indicate that PIs are members of an EHA SWG or include a letter of endorsement from an EHA SWG Chair.\\nYou must form your consortium within a maximum of one year of the closing date listed above.\\nIf you plan to receive funding in addition to the requested EHA support, you must specify this in your project proposal. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s171\",\"d1\",6773,7041,\"Additional funding can come from public or philanthropic institutions, but it cannot come from industry or for-profit entities.\\nIf you have questions about eligibility, please send us an email at [email protected] before you apply.\\nWhat an EHA Innovation Grant covers\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s172\",\"d1\",7041,7427,\"To reflect the collaborative spirit of the grant, no more than 40% of the total grant should be allocated to one member of the consortium.\\nYou can use your grant for:\\nPersonnel costs, including the applicant or the costs of hiring other research staff to work directly on the project\\nLab consumables\\nSmall equipment\\nMiscellaneous expenses, such as publication of your project’s results\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s173\",\"d1\",7427,7711,\"You must use some of your grant to pay for:\\nAttendance at the EHA Congress whilst your project is active (maximum €2,000 per PI per year)\\nA final audit of your project’s financial costs (maximum €2,000 per PI)\\nYou cannot use your grant to cover:\\nOverhead costs\\nExcessive travel costs\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s174\",\"d1\",7711,8111,\"Costs that are covered by another fund, even if new funding is acquired during the project, that make all or part of the grant redundant\\nIf you acquire additional funding, you must email us at [email protected] about this within 30 days of its awarding. You must also tell us how you’ll use the grants together.\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s175\",\"d1\",8111,8505,\"How to apply for an EHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nJoin EHA\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\n60-day trial\\nGet involved\\nCareer development\\nScientific meetings\\nAbout us\\nMission and vision\\nJobs\\nSponsor EHA\\nContact us\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s176\",\"d1\",8505,8690,\"Follow us\\nPrivacy statement\\nTerms and conditions\\nSubscribe\\nCopyright © 2026\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\\nApply by October 29\\nApply today\",\"document\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"SUPPLY project invol