t\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s187\",\"d1\",3882,4251,\"Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nHome\\nResearch & Innovation\\nGrants\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s188\",\"d1\",4251,4651,\"How to apply for an EHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\\nEHA Travel Grants\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nScope of our grants\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-December 2026.\\nEHA Kick-Off Grants support early-career researchers operating in one of the countries less-represented among EHA grantees. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s189\",\"d1\",4651,5009,\"Successful applicants can receive up to €50,000 for up to two years.\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYou’re operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees (see the full list of eligible countries)\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s190\",\"d1\",5009,5350,\"Your application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nIn addition, at least one of the following must apply:\\nYou received your PhD within eight years of the current closing date\\nYou’re an MD interested in a career in research, and you were awarded your MD or PhD within eight years of the current closing date\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s191\",\"d1\",5350,5729,\"Note: Applicants currently enrolled in a PhD program are not eligible.\\nIf you received your qualifications outside the stated timeframe, please check our policy on life events and eligibility.\\nProposal criteria\\nYour proposal will be eligible if it’s:\\nA new research question that lacks solid preliminary data\\nHypothesis-driven and based on a strong and novel scientific question\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s192\",\"d1\",5729,6042,\"Focused on hypothesis-testing rather than generation\\nAble to achieve results within two years\\nYour application will not be eligible if it:\\nRelates to development of commercial technology (unless there is a solid research question)\\nIs aimed at descriptive molecular profiling\\nIs about other non-lab-based research\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s193\",\"d1\",6042,6426,\"If you have other questions about eligibility, you can contact us at [email protected] before submitting an application.\\nWhat an EHA Kick-Off Grant covers\\nAn EHA Kick-Off Grant covers:\\nPartial salary of the applicant\\nLab consumables\\nEquipment—up to a maximum of € 5,000\\nThe mandatory cost of attending the EHA Congress whilst your project is active—up to a maximum of €2,000 per year\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s194\",\"d1\",6426,6804,\"It does not cover:\\nOverhead costs\\nPersonnel costs (other than the applicant)\\nTravel costs other than to the EHA Congress\\nFunding for existing projects\\nThe development of commercial technology, unless it’s based on a solid research question\\nIf this grant does not fully cover your expenses, you must share details of how you’ll cover them.\\nHow to apply for an EHA Kick-off Grant\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s195\",\"d1\",6804,7200,\"EHA Kick-off Grant Review and Selection Process\\nExtending the reach of EHA Grants\\nShare\\nGrants\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nEHA Innovation Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant\\nHow to apply for an EHA Kick-off Grant\\nEHA Kick-off Grant review and selection process\\nEHA Research Mobility Gr